---
import Shapes from "./Shapes.astro";
---
<section class="section problem">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="panel-field wrap" data-reveal>
      <div class="mesh" aria-hidden="true"><Shapes name="mesh" /></div>
      <div class="inner">
        <h2 class="h2">Raw CLI is the wrong abstraction for AI agents</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          RouterOS is powerful, but asking an LLM to improvise shell commands against production
          network gear is risky. MikroMCP gives agents a controlled tool surface: strict schemas,
          idempotent writes, dry-run previews, per-router circuit breakers, retry policies, RBAC,
          audit logs, snapshots, and rollback-aware change workflows.
        </p>
        <p class="pull mono">
          MikroMCP turns MikroTik RouterOS into a production-minded MCP control plane.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .wrap { padding: 68px 40px 60px; text-align: center; }
  .mesh { position: absolute; inset: 0; opacity: .16; pointer-events: none; }
  .inner { position: relative; max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .lede { margin: 22px auto 0; }
  .pull {
    margin: 30px auto 0; display: inline-block; font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text); padding: 12px 22px; border-radius: 999px;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,.05); border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  }
  @media (max-width: 620px) { .wrap { padding: 44px 22px 42px; } }
</style>
